{
 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "Write the number so that A is between 1 and 10",
   "Count how many places you moved the decimal point",
   "Moving left → positive power; moving right → negative power",
   "For calculations: deal with the A parts and 10^n parts separately"
  ],
  "title": "How to Use Standard Form",
  "content": "<p><strong>Standard form</strong> is \\(A \\times 10^n\\) where \\(1 \\leq A < 10\\) and \\(n\\) is an integer.</p><p><strong>Large numbers:</strong> Move the decimal left until \\(1 \\leq A < 10\\). Count moves = positive \\(n\\).</p><p><strong>Small numbers:</strong> Move the decimal right. Count moves = negative \\(n\\).</p><p><strong>Calculations:</strong> Multiply/divide the \\(A\\) values and add/subtract the powers.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Write 45 600 in standard form</strong></p><p>\\(4.56 \\times 10^4\\) (decimal moved 4 places left)</p>"
 },
